                <pb facs="0448" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg354"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1015.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 1006 of the
                    27th ultimo, I have the honor to inclose herewith statements made yesterday in
                    the House of Commons by Mr. Gardner, president of the board of agriculture, in
                    reply to questions asked by his predecessor, Mr. Chaplin, relative to a recent
                    outbreak of pleuro-pneumonia and to the arrangements made for the examination of
                    Canadian cattle when landed in this country.</p>
                <p>I also inclose two copies of the order of the board of agriculture referred to by
                    Mr. Gardner as having been published in the London Gazette of the 17th
                    ultimo.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d271-a1.xml" xpointer="d271-a1"/>
